Hi David,
I'm not sure about LSM, but I recently replaced a boot disk on my system.
First, I ran a "df" command to check the domain of the boot disk:
# df -k
Filesystem        1024-blocks        Used   Available Capacity  Mounted on
cluster_root#root     5880152      100065     5773992     2%    /
root1_domain#root      262144       39349      217816    16% 
/cluster/members/member1/boot_partition
<snip>

Next, look in the fdmns directory:
# find /etc/fdmns
/etc/fdmns/root1_domain
/etc/fdmns/root1_domain/dsk3a
<snip>

This tell me that the boot disk is dsk3
